# NOTE: you can let Wasp set up your Postgres DB by running `wasp start db` in a separate terminal window.
# then, in a new terminal window, run `wasp db migrate-dev` and finally `wasp start`.
# If you use `wasp start db` then you DO NOT need to add a DATABASE_URL env variable here.
# DATABASE_URL=

# REQUIRED -- Stripe is the only active payment processor (src/payment/paymentProcessor.ts).
# For testing, go to https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys and get a test stripe key that starts with "sk_test_..."
STRIPE_API_KEY=sk_test_...
# After downloading starting the stripe cli (https://stripe.com/docs/stripe-cli) with `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3101/payments-webhook` it will output your signing secret
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# You can find your Stripe customer portal URL in the Stripe Dashboard under the 'Customer Portal' settings.
STRIPE_CUSTOMER_PORTAL_URL=https://billing.stripe.com/...

# REQUIRED -- one real Stripe price id per plan (https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/products,
# + Add Product). getPlanAvailability (src/payment/operations.ts) checks these live and
# shows "Coming soon" on /pricing for any plan still left at the placeholder below --
# there's no separate flag to flip once a real id is set.
PAYMENTS_FAST_TRACK_PLAN_ID=012345
PAYMENTS_STANDARD_PLAN_ID=012345
PAYMENTS_EXTENDED_PLAN_ID=012345
# Ireland Pathway (IDC-only plan) -- only needed once real Stripe checkout is wired for
# it (PRD-002 §6 Q2 launch gate); admin-grant testing doesn't touch this at all.
PAYMENTS_IRELAND_PATHWAY_PLAN_ID=012345

# REQUIRED -- set this as a comma-separated list of emails you want to give admin privileges to upon registeration
ADMIN_EMAILS=me@example.com,you@example.com,them@example.com

# REQUIRED -- account verification and password-reset emails (main.wasp.ts's
# `emailSender`, Wasp 0.25's first-class Resend provider). Get a key at
# https://resend.com/api-keys. Replaced SendGrid (never actually wired up here).
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# REQUIRED -- Amazon S3, for question-review image uploads (src/file-upload/s3Utils.ts).
# Get credentials at https://console.aws.amazon.com and create a new IAM user with S3 access.
AWS_S3_IAM_ACCESS_KEY=ACK...
AWS_S3_IAM_SECRET_KEY=t+33a...
AWS_S3_FILES_BUCKET=your-bucket-name
AWS_S3_REGION=your-region

# OPTIONAL, NOT USED BY ANY FEATURE TODAY -- src/server/ai/claudeClient.ts is a reusable
# Claude client with no callers yet. Only needed if a future feature starts using it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# REQUIRED for the admin "Draft with AI" review suggestions (src/admin/dashboards/questions/aiSuggest.ts,
# OpenAI gpt-4.1-mini). These only ever draft unconfirmed suggestions for a human reviewer, per this
# project's "never invent/auto-publish content" rule (see app/CLAUDE.md). Get a key at
# https://platform.openai.com/account
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# NOT CURRENTLY USED -- OpenSaaS template leftovers with zero live code path in this
# repo. Kept here only so a future re-adoption doesn't have to rediscover the var
# names; delete this whole block if you're confident they'll never be used.
#
# LemonSqueezy: a real, working alternate PaymentProcessor implementation
# (src/payment/lemonSqueezy/) exists but is not the one main.wasp.ts wires up --
# src/payment/paymentProcessor.ts:36 hardcodes Stripe. Only needed if you switch that.
# LEMONSQUEEZY_API_KEY=eyJ...
# LEMONSQUEEZY_STORE_ID=012345
# LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=my-webhook-secret
#
# Google social auth: main.wasp.ts's `auth.methods` only configures email+password
# today, no `google: {}` entry -- these vars are inert until that's added.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=722...
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOC...
#
# Plausible analytics (server-side reporting API) and Google Analytics (server-side
# reporting API, distinct from the client-side REACT_APP_GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID in
# .env.client, which cookie-consent/Config.ts does actually read) -- no server code
# reads any of the four vars below today.
# PLAUSIBLE_API_KEY=gUTgtB...
# PLAUSIBLE_SITE_ID=yoursite.com
# PLAUSIBLE_BASE_URL=https://plausible.io/api
# GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_CLIENT_EMAIL=email@example.gserviceaccount.com
# GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_PRIVATE_KEY=LS02...
# GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_PROPERTY_ID=123456789
